# C# Testing Best Practices

Use **xUnit** with Clean Architecture testing strategies. Prefer **NSubstitute** for mocks.

## Project Structure

```
tests/
├── unit/
│   └── MyApp.UnitTests/
│       ├── Domain/
│       │   ├── Entities/
│       │   └── ValueObjects/
│       └── Application/
│           └── UseCases/
└── integration/
    └── MyApp.IntegrationTests/
        └── Infrastructure/
```

Mirror `src/` layer structure under unit and integration test projects.

## Testing by Layer

### Domain Layer

Pure unit tests. No mocks — entities and value objects are self-contained.

```csharp
public sealed class EmailTests
{
    [Fact]
    public void Constructor_ValidEmail_SetsValue()
    {
        var email = new Email("user@example.com");
        Assert.Equal("user@example.com", email.Value);
    }

    [Theory]
    [InlineData("")]
    [InlineData("not-an-email")]
    public void Constructor_InvalidEmail_Throws(string value)
    {
        Assert.Throws<ArgumentException>(() => new Email(value));
    }
}
```

### Application Layer

Unit tests with mocked ports (NSubstitute).

```csharp
using NSubstitute;

public sealed class CreateUserUseCaseTests
{
    [Fact]
    public async Task ExecuteAsync_ValidInput_SavesUser()
    {
        var repo = Substitute.For<IUserRepository>();
        repo.SaveAsync(Arg.Any<User>(), Arg.Any<CancellationToken>())
            .Returns(call => call.Arg<User>());

        var useCase = new CreateUserUseCase(repo);

        var user = await useCase.ExecuteAsync("john@example.com", "John");

        Assert.Equal("john@example.com", user.Email.Value);
        await repo.Received(1).SaveAsync(
            Arg.Is<User>(u => u.Email.Value == "john@example.com"),
            Arg.Any<CancellationToken>());
    }
}
```

### Infrastructure Layer

Integration tests against real dependencies when needed. Prefer Testcontainers for databases and other external services.

Keep unit tests free of I/O, network, and real databases.

## Naming

Use `Method_Scenario_Expected` (or `Method_WhenX_ShouldY`):

```csharp
// ✅ Good
public void GetById_WhenMissing_ReturnsNull() { }

// ❌ Bad
public void Test1() { }
public void GetUserWorks() { }
```

## Commands

```bash
# All tests
dotnet test

# Specific project
dotnet test tests/unit/MyApp.UnitTests

# Filter by fully qualified name
dotnet test --filter "FullyQualifiedName~CreateUserUseCase"

# Filter by trait (when used)
dotnet test --filter "Category=Unit"
```

## Guidelines

- Unit tests: in-memory only, fast, isolated
- One behavior per test; arrange–act–assert
- Prefer `[Theory]` + `[InlineData]` over duplicated `[Fact]`s for input variants
- Do not call real HTTP APIs or production databases from unit tests
